  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Roads for Development Program Phase Two in Vanuatu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment is to support Vanuatu&apos;s Ministry of Infrastructure and Public Utilities and Public Works Department (PWD) to positively influence road-funding outcomes and use enhanced institutional capacity to manage and develop Vanuatu&apos;s road network more effectively and efficiently. The key activities of the investment include physical civil works and institutional capacity development in areas such as civil works, procurement, systems and human resources. Its engineers help PWD counterparts to plan and implement its annual road operations work plan, including road works directly funded by Australia through a Direct Funding Arrangement. Technical specialists in financial management, procurement, information systems, organizational development and GEDSI to work with government counterparts to strengthen PWD&apos;s &apos;business&apos; as a road network manager.</narrative>
  </description>
